@node about "what the hell is this shit about"
PURPOSE:

i wrote this security system because my bbs was bothered by some hack
attacks. nevermind the hacker was kimble. ok .. what to do with a system
with 8 users accessing useredit, exorcist, axedit, maintenance utils...
[i recommend for this kind of actions a userlevel of 255!]
the idea of the `yuelden security system` was born.

this util consists of two XIM doors.. you may add them both to your
bbs.cmd (or even as an icon .. i will NOT explain how to install this
on /X3.xx bbs` cause i REALLY DISlike this shit but you`ll make it for
sure) or better (like i did) add the YSS util to your SYS.CMD (for more
information click on @{"INSTALLATION" link install} and the ID util to
your bbs.cmd.

the YSS util will reduce the level of ANY user logging in with an
userlevel of 255 to a level of your decision...
the ID util will do the opposite and will INCREASE the userlevel of an
cosysop for example up to 255 [after entering 2 passwords of your choice]

so there will be a 1oo% securitry for your system so that even if a hacker
will hack YOUR or one of your co`s accounts no damage can be done by this
SHIThead cause he`ll never hack your 2 (!) special passwords...

let it be written ... let it be done ... i`m sent here by the stoned one...

@endnode
@node contents "gosh! what is in this damned archieve ?"
CONTENTS:

fILE_iD.dIZ    -   370 bytes - upload description given by author
id             - 11100 bytes - identifier xim module [levelINCREASER]
yss            - 10252 bytes - yuelden security system xim module [DECREASER]
security.guide - 11216 bytes - this guidefile

please note that if you are an ß-tester the file length of 'yss' might differ.

@endnode
@node requirements "and what must i have to run this..."
REQUIREMENTS:

> installed s-express or /X [no matter which version]
> some experience in using amiga dos and installing doors to your bbs
> an iq of more than 23
> a real huge dick       o o
> at least some cosysops  |
                         \_/

don`t blame me if this xim module will *NOT* run on your system.
i`m running a amiga4ooo/3o with 6 mb ram and sigma express o.36ß, but
i think this fine util will run on ANY MACHINE with any kind of /X or
s-express versions.

N O  M O R E  system ^ /Xversion dependent utils !!!

@endnode
@node install "iiyes.. at least the installation procedure"
INSTALLATION:

no need of panic ... just very simple to install...

first  : you HAVE TO create a directory in your doors: directory called
         YUELDEN. (please DO this else the doors WON`T work, but i`m pretty
         sure you`ll find that out yourself...)

second : copy all the files included in the archive (you may delete the
         boring bbs adds of hundreds of bbs`) to DOORS:YUELDEN/

third  : we take berlin

fourth : add the following to your sys.cmd (or even to your shitty icons)
         yss       XS001doors:yuelden/yss

fifth  : add the following to your bbs.cmd (blablabla)
         *id       XM066doors:yuelden/id
                      ^^
         this should be your STANDARD cosysop (eall?!) level 
fifth  : add the following to your bbs:bull.txt
         ~CC_yss|
         but i think you`re man enuff to call a door via mci on your OWN!

sixth  : ok .. just two things to do ... cause i really HATE using lame
         config files i decided to use the files` FILECOMMENT as a config
         line. so the filecomment line for the YSS util consists of the
         level which is given to THE user logging on with a level of 255
         (-i-really-can-kill-yar-bbs-) instead of this level...

seventh: the filecomment line for the ID util consists of the two passwords
         needed by the user to IDENTIFY HIMSELF for YOUR system ...
         [separated by the "°" [ascii 176] just type
         LIST DOORS:YUELDEN
         to watch the examples given by the author (iiiyes .. that`s ME!)

@endnode
@node howto "help! how can i use this..."
HOW TO USE:

after reading @{"INSTALLATION" link install} it should be NO prob for you
to know HOW to use this but i`m willing to explain it AGAIN! (and again
and again..)

by adding the following line to your BBS:BULL.TXT (the text that is shown
to the user right when he enters your bbs)

~CC_yss|

every user that logs on with an level of 255 will be SLAVED down to a level
of your choice...

add the custom command ID to your bbs.cmd as it`s described at
@{"INSTALLATION" link install}. (that`s the one which will make 'them' able
to gain their sysop status again.

if there are still some probs feel free to contact me or any other yuelden
team member in this bloody world... [yes... you HAVE to watch the greets
and adds]
@endnode
